  "booster": {
    "name": "Play Booster",
    "description": "14 cards: 7 commons (in 4.2% of the boosters one is a scene card, and in 1 of 28 a source material card replaces one), 2 uncommons (in 3.9% of the boosters one is a scene card, in 7.8% a sewer frame card), a legendary Turtle of any rarity (a common 64.1%, an uncommon 13.1%, a rare 6.9%, a mythic rare 3.4%; a scene common 4.6%, uncommon 6.5% or rare 1%; or a silhouette mythic rare), a wildcard of any rarity (a common 24.9%, an uncommon 62.1%, a rare 7.6%, a scene uncommon 1.3%, a sewer frame uncommon 2.6%, or a mythic rare, a scene common or rare, a sewer frame rare or mythic rare or a silhouette mythic rare), a rare (84.9%) or mythic rare (9.2%) or a sewer frame rare (4.1%), a scene rare, a sewer frame mythic rare or a silhouette mythic rare, a traditional foil of any rarity (a common 61.5%, an uncommon 27.7%, a rare 6.7%, or a mythic rare, a scene, sewer frame or silhouette card) and a land (a common dual land 48%, foil 12%; a rooftop basic 32%, foil 8%). The legendary Turtle cards (Jennika and the four brothers' cards) appear only in their own slot and the foil slot, as the published counts of the common and uncommon slots show; the replacement odds of the common and uncommon slots are read as per booster. Published only as less than 1%, so derived: what is left to 100% in a slot is shared evenly among the treatments published as less than 1% (the legendary Turtle slot's silhouettes 0.4%; the wildcard's six 0.25% each; the rare slot's three 0.6% each; the foil's eight 0.5125% each). Each booster also holds a double-sided token, which isn't a game card.",
